course: dictionary
lesson: 8308
title: Roadside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The roadside is the ground at the edge of a road. When roadside comes before a noun, it describes something beside a road, like a roadside stall.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Poppies grow in disturbed soil, so they come up on fields and roadsides after digging.» Fields and roadsides are places, so roadsides must be the edges of roads where plants can grow.
explain: Try the swap check. Put beside a road in place of roadside. «Pick berries away from roads, and wash the roadside ones before eating» still makes sense, so roadside means beside a road.
fact: Roadside is a noun in «the roadside» and an adjective in «a roadside café».
fact: «Roadside» means the edge of a road, or something beside a road.
fact: «Roadsides» can be home to wildflowers and insects.
fact: «Roadside» zoos are not always checked, so accredited zoos are safer to visit.
fact: Useful phrases: by the roadside, at the roadside, roadside rubbish, a roadside stall.
exercise: «Poppies grow on fields and roadsides after digging.» In this sentence, what is a roadside? | A pepper pot | A kind of car | *The edge of a road, where plants can grow | The middle of a motorway
exercise: «Pick berries away from roads, because roadside ones may be polluted by traffic fumes.» What does roadside mean in roadside ones? | Berries picked by children | Berries that are sweet and red | *Berries growing beside a road | Berries sold in a shop
exercise: Which phrase describes a stall beside a road? | an indoor swimming pool | *a roadside stall | a sandy beach | a quiet kitchen
test: If a car breaks down, where should people wait? | *At the roadside, away from traffic | In the middle of the road | Under the car | On the motorway
test: In «a roadside stall», what kind of word is roadside? | *An adjective | A noun only | A full stop | A verb
exam: Which sentence uses roadside as a noun? | *The flowers grew at the roadside | Roadside berries may be dirty | A roadside café opened last week | The roadside stall sold apples
